`@ReturnsMutableObject` was incorrectly applied to `getAsJson()`, which constructs and returns a new `JsonObject` rather than exposing an internal mutable field.

## Change

- **`SGCustomProperty.getAsJson()`** — removed `@ReturnsMutableObject` annotation; the method always returns a freshly created instance, so the annotation was misleading to callers and static analysis tools.

```java
// Before
@NonNull
@ReturnsMutableObject
public IJsonObject getAsJson ()

// After
@NonNull
public IJsonObject getAsJson ()
```

